From 8cd4c91887ea361302dd6438ea00e6e745726a9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:48:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] perf(adaptive): simplify growth outlines before opening

Thin each opening input at the existing 0.25 um arc tolerance to avoid
repeated offsets of the growth planner's fine join vertices. Use an
explicit stack, retain the original outline when normalization changes
its loop or hole counts, and clip every opened result to its original
region after a 0.51 um extra erosion.

Keep all load, crossing, kink and geometry-budget laws unchanged. Pin
whole-region containment on narrow and nested outlines, bound charged
growth vertices on a fine rounded slot, and remeasure the adaptive
fixtures and the actual STEP bore in release and debug. Record the
measured Linux path triple and the unmeasured platform limitation.

Co-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-6 Astra) <noreply@openai.com>

Fixes #882
